@startuml
title ioScope Object View
skinparam shadowing false

object controller as "controller : ioOscilloscopeController"
object model as "model : ioOscilloscopeModel"
object qtWindow as "qtWindow : ioQtScopeWindow"
object compactView as "compactView : ioCompactOscilloscopeView"
object detailedView as "detailedView : ioDetailedOscilloscopeView"
object controlState as "controlState : ioControlState"
object viewportState as "viewportState : ioViewportState"
object filterPipeline as "filterPipeline : ioFilterPipeline"
object waveformGenerator as "waveformGenerator : ioWaveformGenerator"
object dataBuffer as "dataBuffer : ioDataBuffer"
object readWorker as "readWorker : ioUsbReadController"
object writeWorker as "writeWorker : ioUsbWriteController"

qtWindow --> controller
qtWindow --> compactView
qtWindow --> detailedView
controller --> model
controller --> compactView
controller --> detailedView
model --> controlState
model --> viewportState
model --> filterPipeline
model --> waveformGenerator
readWorker --> dataBuffer
writeWorker --> dataBuffer

note over qtWindow, detailedView
One abstract View contract exists in the class design.
This object view shows two concrete Qt view instances
hosted by the Qt window.
end note

note bottom of dataBuffer
This runtime object is the single shared circular buffer
used by the implemented producer-consumer path.
end note
@enduml
